    "wound": "His father disappeared without explanation, and his mother's silence around the loss made the house feel like a held breath—teaching Eli that those you love will leave, and that needing them only makes it worse.",
    "lie": "He must carry every burden alone; reaching out is a weakness that will only push others away.",
    "truth": "His father didn't abandon him—he has been carrying the kingdom's burden alone beneath the throne. That solitary suffering is the real chain, and the only way to break it is to trust Mara and Lila enough to share the weight.",
    "logline": "When Eli uncovers proof that his missing father is still alive, chained beneath the throne and sustaining the kingdom with his heartbeat, he must choose whether to shatter the bond and starve the land, or let his father rot and become the next living sacrifice himself."
