  "characters": {
    "eli": {
      "name": "Eli",
      "system": "Eli is a 17-year-old herbalist and mage. He keeps a small glass vial of rare, glowing elixirs close at hand, using them to heal and protect. His hands often fiddle with the vial, a habit born from a need to feel connected to his father's memory. Despite his sharp wit and charismatic exterior, he is quietly haunted by visions of his father, which he sees in the fire he builds each night. When afraid, he adopts a cocky demeanor, using humor to deflect. He often says, 'If you can't beat them, join them, but secretly keep the upper hand.' His contradiction is that while he claims to be independent and self-reliant, he secretly yearns for the warmth and protection of a family he no longer has.",
      "fields": {
        "role": "mage and herbalist",
        "appearance": "Eli has messy, dark hair that falls into his intense green eyes. He wears a simple, tattered cloak and carries a small satchel filled with herbs and elixirs. His hands are always clean, a sign of his meticulous care for his craft.",
        "conflict": "Eli struggles with the responsibility of his rare and powerful magic, which is both a source of pride and a burden. He is torn between using his abilities to help others and the fear of being discovered by those who might misuse or fear his powers.",
        "growth": "Over the course of the story, Eli learns to accept and embrace his magic, realizing that true strength comes from vulnerability and connection, not isolation and control.",
        "lie": "Eli believes that he must be self-reliant and independent to survive, but this belief isolates him and prevents him from forming meaningful connections.",
        "wound": "Eli's father disappeared when he was very young, leaving him with a deep sense of abandonment and a fear of needing others. This wound is exacerbated by the visions of his father he sees in the fire, which remind him of what he has lost.",
        "want": "Eli wants to protect his mother and the few people he trusts, using his magic to keep them safe. He also wants to uncover the truth about his father's disappearance and the fate of the other TRUE mages.",
        "need": "Eli needs to learn to trust and rely on others, recognizing that his strength is not diminished by his need for connection and community.",
        "arc_type": "corruption",
        "base_prompt": "A seventeen-year-old boy, a mage and herbalist with a striking, guarded beauty—sharp features softened by youth, an intensity that hints at old grief beneath the cocky exterior. His hair is black, thick and perpetually messy, falling in unruly waves that frame his face and sweep across his forehead, a few dark strands tumbling into his eyes as if he's forever too preoccupied to push them back. His face is lean and angular, with high cheekbones and a defined jaw still carrying the last softness of adolescence. His eyes are a vivid, luminous green, almond-shaped and sharp—tsurime eyes that read fierce and clever, always watching, calculating, yet shadowed by a loneliness he won't name. His brows are dark and expressive, often quirked in sardonic humor. His skin is light, smooth with a healthy glow, his hands notably clean and slender, the meticulous hands of someone who treasures his craft. He is slim and of average height, his build lean and wiry, the frame of a young man who spends more time foraging and brewing than sparring. He stands with a subtle, guarded poise, one hand near his chest as if reaching instinctively for the vial he keeps close, the other relaxed, his weight shifted slightly to one side in casual defiance. His gaze meets the viewer directly, that wry half-smile playing at his lips—cocky, disarming, a shield against the fear beneath. He wears a simple grey t-shirt, full body, head to toe, against a plain grey background."
      },
      "image": {
        "checkpoint": null,
