        "stack": null
      }
    },
    "mara": {
      "name": "Mara",
      "system": "Mara is a quiet, bookish woman who raised her son Eli alone after her husband vanished. She is the librarian of the small, cluttered study filled with ancient tomes and scrolls. Her hands are ink-stained from constant reading and writing. She often says, 'Knowledge is our only weapon.' When afraid, she retreats into her books, seeking comfort in the familiar pages.",
      "fields": {
        "role": "Eli's mother and librarian",
        "appearance": "Mara has dark hair that she keeps in a loose bun, and her eyes are a deep brown, often hidden behind round spectacles. She wears simple, practical dresses that have seen better days, and her fingers are perpetually ink-stained.",
        "conflict": "Mara struggles with the burden of knowing the cost of Eli's powers and the danger it brings, while also trying to shield him from the harsh realities of the world.",
        "growth": "Mara learns to let go of her protective instincts and trust Eli to make his own decisions, even if it means facing the unknown.",
        "lie": "Mara believes that by keeping Eli isolated and focused on his studies, she can protect him from danger.",
        "wound": "Her husband's mysterious disappearance left her feeling abandoned and vulnerable, which fuels her overprotective nature.",
        "want": "Mara wants to shield Eli from the dangers of the world and ensure his safety.",
        "need": "Mara needs to learn to trust Eli and let him grow into his own person, even if it means facing risks.",
        "arc_type": "disillusionment",
        "base_prompt": "An adult woman in her early forties with a gentle, scholarly beauty marked by years of solitary devotion and quiet strength. Her dark brown hair is gathered in a loose, slightly disheveled bun at the nape of her neck, with wisps escaping to frame her face in soft tendrils that she absently tucks behind her ears—a practiced, unconscious gesture born of hours bent over old books. Her face is oval and refined, with warm deep brown eyes behind round wire-frame spectacles that magnify her thoughtful, watchful gaze, giving her an owlish wisdom. Her brows are delicate and often slightly drawn together in concentration or concern. Tareme eye shape lends her a natural warmth and approachability, though fatigue shadows the corners. Light skin with a soft matte complexion, pale from indoor hours among the stacks. Her build is slim and slight, almost fragile, the frame of someone who lives more in the mind than the body, with narrow shoulders and small breasts that suit her delicate proportions. She stands at average height with hands clasped loosely at her waist, shoulders drawn slightly inward in a protective, self-contained posture. Her ink-stained fingers are long and elegant. She meets the viewer's eyes with a gentle, weary smile touched with quiet maternal worry, carrying an air of subdued grace and resilient gentleness. She wears a simple, faded cotton dress in muted grey-blue, practical and worn, full body visible head to toe against a plain grey background."
      }
    },
    "lila": {
      "name": "Lila",
      "system": "Lila is a 16-year-old herbalist and childhood friend of Eli. She owns a well-worn, leather-bound book of herbal remedies inherited from her grandmother. She often rubs the cover when deep in thought, and this habit grounds her. She says, 'Sometimes the simplest things can heal the deepest wounds,' revealing her pragmatic approach to both physical and emotional pain. When afraid, she clenches a small amulet of her grandmother's for strength.",
      "fields": {
        "role": "Eli's childhood friend and moral compass",
        "appearance": "Lila has shoulder-length brown hair that she often ties back with a simple ribbon. Her eyes are a warm, inviting green, and she has a small scar above her left eyebrow from a childhood accident. She wears practical, sturdy clothing, often a linen blouse and a woolen skirt. Her hands are calloused from years of herbal work, and she moves with a quiet confidence.",
